# Fear of Burning Alive's delirium ability needs four card types among cards in its controller's graveyard and noncombat damage to
# an opponent (CR 120.2, 603.4). Turn 1: Bot1 casts an Ornithopter and three Moxen and pays Wheel of Fortune with Black Lotus,
# so the graveyard holds Black Lotus (artifact), the Wheel (sorcery) and a discarded Island (land): three types, one short.
# Turn 3 Fear's enters trigger deals 4 to Bot2 and the delirium ability does not trigger (the stack is empty). Turn 5 a Lightning
# Bolt to Bot2's face does not trigger it either (the Bolt is still on the stack, not in the graveyard); with the Bolt in the graveyard
# there are four types, and a second Bolt dealing 3 to Bot2's Steel Wall does not trigger it (a creature is not an opponent), nor does
# Fear's own combat damage to Bot2 (combat damage is not noncombat damage).

